-- title:
--   Volume of a half-closed cube of side $h$
-- statement:
--   For a real number $h$ and a point $u \in \mathbb{R}^d$, let
--   $\tilde{A}_h(u) := \texttt{halfClosedCube } h\ u$ be the half-closed axis-parallel cube of side $h$
--   attached to $u$ — the variant that is closed on one side and open on the other in each coordinate,
--   so that the cubes indexed by the scaled lattice $h\mathbb{Z}^d$ tile $\mathbb{R}^d$ exactly. Let
--   $h \ge 0$. Then
--
--   $$\lambda_d\big(\tilde{A}_h(u)\big) \;=\; h^{d},$$
--
--   as an element of $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   The half-closed cubes are the tiles that make every point of $\mathbb{R}^d$ lie in exactly one
--   cube, which is what defines the step index and hence the whole discretisation; this lemma says that
--   passing from the closed cube to the half-closed one costs nothing in measure, so the two may be
--   interchanged inside any integral.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The hypothesis is $h \ge 0$, so the degenerate mesh $h = 0$ is permitted;
--   the right-hand side is `ENNReal.ofReal (h ^ d)`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/LebesgueDiff.lean#L311-L322

